{"name":"Mint Condition","hex":"#dffbf3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mint condition","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The condition of newness or perfection, as if just freshly minted."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mint_condition"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mint Condition","blocks":[{"text":"Mint Condition is an American R&B band from St. Paul, Minnesota.\nThe band is focused on diverse genres such as jazz, hip hop, funk and dance. Mint Condition has also been nominated for one Grammy and three Soul Train Awards. The group is credited with being one of the last major funk bands to chart before hip-hop and new jack swing dominated black music in the 1990s."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/140218-F-VU439-187_American_R_%26_B_band_Mint_Condition_at_Transit_Center_at_Manas%2C_Kyrgyzstan%2C_2014.jpg/330px-140218-F-VU439-187_American_R_%26_B_band_Mint_Condition_at_Transit_Center_at_Manas%2C_Kyrgyzstan%2C_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mint_Condition","wikidata":"Q6869552"},{"title":"Mint condition","blocks":[{"text":"Mint condition is an expression used to denote the quality of a pre-owned good as displaying virtually no imperfections and being in pristine condition relative to its original production state. Originally, the phrase related to the way collectors described the condition of coins. As the name given to a coin factory is a \"mint\", then mint condition is the condition a coin is in when it leaves the mint."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/BlackBuick1938HoodUpDok1.jpg/330px-BlackBuick1938HoodUpDok1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mint_condition","wikidata":"Q6869578"},{"title":"Spring green","blocks":[{"text":"Spring green is a color that was traditionally considered to be on the yellow side of green, but in modern computer systems based on the RGB color model is halfway between cyan and green on the color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/%D0%97%D2%AF%D0%BC%D1%96%D1%80%D0%B5%D1%82.jpg/330px-%D0%97%D2%AF%D0%BC%D1%96%D1%80%D0%B5%D1%82.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_green","wikidata":"Q373787"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Green_vintage_buttons.jpg/500px-Green_vintage_buttons.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Green_vintage_buttons.jpg/500px-Green_vintage_buttons.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGreen_vintage_buttons.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Common_Green_Magpie_the_emerald_phantom_lighting_the_ancient_forests_of_the_Himalayas_01.jpg/500px-Common_Green_Magpie_the_emerald_phantom_lighting_the_ancient_forests_of_the_Himalayas_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Common_Green_Magpie_the_emerald_phantom_lighting_the_ancient_forests_of_the_Himalayas_01.jpg/500px-Common_Green_Magpie_the_emerald_phantom_lighting_the_ancient_forests_of_the_Himalayas_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACommon_Green_Magpie_the_emerald_phantom_lighting_the_ancient_forests_of_the_Himalayas_01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/D%C3%BCsseldorf%2C_Schadowplatz%2C_Enzi-B%C3%A4nke%2C_1._April_2014_%2811%29.jpg/500px-D%C3%BCsseldorf%2C_Schadowplatz%2C_Enzi-B%C3%A4nke%2C_1._April_2014_%2811%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wi